## Redis / KV Patterns

Use `kv` from `@/lib/kv` (Upstash Redis / Vercel KV).

### Key patterns in use — never conflict with these:
| Key | Value | Purpose |
|-----|-------|---------|
| `sub:{email}` | `{ plan, status, trialEnd }` | User subscription |
| `workflow:{id}` | `WorkflowRecord` | Saved workflow |
| `workflows:{email}` | list of IDs | User's workflow index |
| `workflow-runs:{email}` | number | Trial run counter |
| `telegram-chatid:{email}` | string | Saved Telegram chat ID |
| `telegram-verify:{code}` | string (chatId) | Temp verification code (10min TTL) |
| `slack-webhook:{email}` | string | Saved Slack webhook URL |
| `whatsapp-config:{email}` | JSON string | Twilio or Meta credentials |
| `slug:{slug}` | siteId | Site slug index |
| `site:{id}` | SiteRecord | Generated site |
| `sites:{email}` | list of IDs | User's sites index |

```typescript
import { kv } from '@/lib/kv'
const val = await kv.get<MyType>('key')
await kv.set('key', value)
await kv.del('key')
```

